ףFװה¶‰ßyחשQ]Q!£™OÙsk¹§ד¿¼׀.ֻ<{"url":"/gcsl/embedding/embedding/","fragment":{"page_number":0,"data":{"url":"/gcsl/embedding/embedding/","content":"Embedding GCSL. The gcsl Rust crate exposes the language pipeline without requiring the command-line program. You can evaluate one source, retain an interactive session, or load a workspace supplied by your application. Choosing the boundary # The repository separates four responsibilities: CrateResponsibility gcsl. Syntax, types, evaluation, formatting, and semantic indexing. gcsl-disk. Finding workspace roots and reading source trees. gcsl-lsp. Editor protocol, document state, and request handling. gcsl-cli. Command arguments, terminal interaction, and output. gcsl::run evaluates a SourceFile as a standalone program. A Session retains names and values across inputs. workspace::Workspace evaluates selected files after a workspace check. The lower-level lexer, parser, checker, and index are available when you only need a particular stage. Consult the Rust API documentation for exact signatures and ownership. Stack and lifetime # Run the language pipeline on a thread with at least gcsl::STACK_SIZE bytes of stack, as the CLI does. Its configured size is 64 MiB. Parsing, checking, lowering, and evaluation share documented nesting limits; a host thread's default stack is not a substitute for the required reservation. Keep the source collection and diagnostic input numbering together. Standard-library files participate in the source list, so diagnostics can point into a helper as well as into user text. The library returns warnings with successful results instead of printing them. A workspace or session owns memoization state and temporary directories. Dropping it performs normal temporary-directory cleanup. Do not return a path to such a directory and then destroy its owner before a consumer has used it. Effects are host effects # The standard library is embedded in the binary. Its process and file operations still run with the embedding process's permissions and resources. The library does not impose a wall-clock limit or turn pure checking into an execution sandbox. A host that accepts untrusted programs needs an external isolation and resource policy. Use gcsl-disk when you want the CLI's workspace-discovery behavior. Supply sources yourself when your host has a different storage model; keep the language's dependency and scope rules intact.","word_count":333,"filters":{},"meta":{"crumbs":"GCSL / Embedding GCSL","title":"Embedding GCSL"},"anchors":[{"element":"h2","id":"choosing-the-boundary","text":"Choosing the boundary #","location":32},{"element":"h2","id":"stack-and-lifetime","text":"Stack and lifetime #","location":123},{"element":"h2","id":"effects-are-host-effects","text":"Effects are host effects #","location":249}]}},"word_data":{"can":[{"position":16,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":191,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"turn":[{"position":285,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"temporari":[{"position":221,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":227,"weight":12,"original_word":null}],"processs":[{"position":272,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"workspacediscoveri":[{"position":312,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"oper":[{"position":266,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"stage":[{"position":112,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"standard":[{"position":182,"weight":12,"original_word":null},{"position":255,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"path":[{"position":233,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"storag":[{"position":323,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"argument":[{"position":68,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"editor":[{"position":59,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"gcsllsp":[{"position":58,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"workspac":[{"position":27,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":52,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":89,"weight":12,"original_word":null},{"position":89,"weight":12,"original_word":null},{"pos